          "type": "plan",
          "text": "# Fix: Gift card email dropdown doesn't update after editing selected value\n\n## Context\n\nPR #6495 added the ability to type custom email addresses in the gift card customer select field. However, there's a remaining bug: after selecting a custom email (e.g. \"Use email: foo@bar.com\"), if the user edits the input to a different email (e.g. `foo-bar@bar.com`), the form still submits with the originally selected email.\n\n**Root cause:** In `GiftCardCustomerSelectField`, `onInputValueChange` only updates `inputValue` (used for search/options) but never clears `selectedCustomer`. The `selectedCustomer` state — which is what gets submitted — remains stale with the old email. The user sees the new typed value in the input but the underlying state doesn't match.\n\nCompare with `CustomerEditForm` (orders) which uses `value={null}` and immediately calls `onCustomerEdit` + `toggleEditMode` on select, avoiding this class of bug entirely.\n\n## Fix\n\n**File:** `src/giftCards/GiftCardCreateDialog/GiftCardCustomerSelectField.tsx`\n\nIn the `onInputValueChange` handler (line 104-107), clear `selectedCustomer` when the input value changes and differs from the currently selected email. This forces the user to re-select from the dropdown, which is the correct UX — they must explicitly pick the new \"Use email: foo-bar@bar.com\" option.\n\n```tsx\nonInputValueChange={val => {\n  setInputValue(val);\n  debouncedSearch(val);\n\n  // Clear selection when user edits the input after selecting\n  if (selectedCustomer.email && val !== selectedCustomer.email) {\n    setSelectedCustomer({ email: \"\", name: \"\" });\n  }\n}}\n```\n\n**File:** `src/giftCards/GiftCardCreateDialog/GiftCardCustomerSelectField.test.tsx`\n\nAdd a test verifying that editing the input after selection clears the selected customer. This requires rendering the component (or at minimum testing the callback logic).\n\n## Verification\n\n1. `pnpm run test:quiet src/giftCards/GiftCardCreateDialog/GiftCardCustomerSelectField.test.tsx`\n2. `pnpm run check-types`\n3. `pnpm run lint`\n4. Manual: open gift card create dialog, type email, select \"Use email\", edit input, confirm selection is cleared\n",
